Id: acc026w
Severity: WARN
Category: accounts
Check: check_accounts
Fix: chmod 750 the home directory (or 700); set HOME_MODE 0750 in login.defs for new accounts.
References: chmod(1); login.defs(5), HOME_MODE and UMASK; CIS Ubuntu Linux 24.04 LTS Benchmark v2.0.0, 7.2.9 (Ensure local interactive user home directories are configured)
Controls: CIS 3.3, 5.1; NIST AC-2, AC-3; ISO 5.16, 5.18, 8.3; CE User access control

The home directory of the listed login ID may be read or searched by
everyone: its mode gives others read or execute permission, so any
other user of the host can list it, open the files in it that are
themselves readable (most are, under the usual umask of 022), and
follow paths through it. CIS asks that an interactive user's home be
750 or stricter; the mode also has to be, or a user's keys, mail and
history are everyone's to read. Debian 12 and later make homes 700
(adduser's DIR_MODE), Ubuntu since 21.04 750 (DIR_MODE and login.defs'
HOME_MODE), Fedora 700 (HOME_MODE) and Arch 700 (UMASK 077); Alpine's
busybox adduser makes them 2755, and hosts upgraded from Debian 11,
Ubuntu 20.04 and earlier keep the 755 those made, as do homes made by
hand: those are what this finds. Write permission for the group or for
others is acc006w. Root and the accounts from UID_MIN (login.defs;
else 1000, or 500 on macOS) up are judged, when they have a login shell
and a home that exists; the system's accounts share homes by design
and are not.
